[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Read the reports and it
holds three problems. Each needs its own fix, so each has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix will not close #4471. The booking-v3 form and the one-day move keep
coming in after it ships.
</Callout>

## What is in #4471

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: day and month swap (7 April becomes 4 July). The tenant writes the day first,
  and the report did not come through booking-v3's form.
- **`hint`**: the same swap, but through booking-v3's form. The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the
  date field; people type what it says and the form reads it day first. Fixing the parser does
  not touch this: the hint is wrong.
- **`shift`**: no swap. The date lands one day early (Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May), or
  depends on where the reader is (Lisbon gets Tuesday, Toronto gets Monday). A date with no time
  is stored as midnight UTC and shown in the viewer's time zone. The desk already lists these
  reports in `desk-notes.json`; this page counts them as their own problem.

Intake's `parser` / `hint` tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. It disagrees with the
tenant on many reports, so the table above places reports by tenant and form, never by tag.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports with the same subject line.
All three problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so
subject matching put them in one ticket. Merging by cause, as the [triage explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe)
already does, keeps them apart.

